{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-faf168c3-d9db-4fa2-85c6-9d8d0cfa2c58","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf20d3d0f9e512fa","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9008-12an3_z7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9008-E003.md","content":"# Identify and prioritize the enterprise tools behind the integration feedback\n\n## Description\n\nThe strategy asks that RHOAI \"integrate better\" with existing enterprise\ntooling, but no specific tools were named in the consolidated feedback. The\ntarget tool set determines everything downstream: which components and teams\nthe integration work touches, whether it is authentication, source control,\nCI, ticketing, data platforms, or ML tooling, and whether the work is even on\nthe affected components listed in the strategy. This investigation names the\ntools, weighs the demand behind each, inventories RHOAI's existing integration\npoints, and produces a prioritized, ratified target-tool list. Its outcome\ndetermines which integration implementation epics exist and what they do, and\ngrounds the enterprise-tooling guidance in the usability whitepaper.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Consolidate all integration-related feedback from strategic accounts and\n  field channels into a single record with per-account attribution, extracting\n  every concrete tool or system mention.\n- Engage field teams and account owners to name the specific enterprise tools\n  behind the general \"integrate better\" statements (for example: identity\n  providers, source control, CI systems, ticketing/work management, data\n  platforms, model/ML tooling), since the consolidated feedback names none.\n- Inventory RHOAI's existing enterprise integration points (for example\n  OpenShift OAuth for authentication and project-scoped RBAC, workbench source\n  control integration) from the platform's documentation and architecture\n  context, and identify the gaps relative to the named tools.\n- For each candidate tool, assess demand weight (how many accounts, which\n  strategic accounts), the rough integration surface, and the platform\n  component that would primarily own the work.\n- Produce a prioritized target-tool list, ratified by product/stakeholder\n  owners, with per-tool rationale, demand evidence, and the platform surface\n  each integration would touch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- All integration-related feedback is consolidated into a single document with\n  per-account attribution and any concrete tool mentions extracted.\n- A named candidate tool list exists with per-account demand evidence and a\n  rough integration surface assessment for each tool.\n- RHOAI's existing enterprise integration points are inventoried, with gaps\n  identified relative to the named tools.\n- A prioritized target-tool list is ratified by product/stakeholder owners,\n  identifying for each tool the platform component the integration would\n  primarily touch — in enough detail to scope implementation epics.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (the platform should integrate better with existing enterprise\n  tooling — no tools named): this investigation resolves which tools HLR-3\n  actually refers to. Implementation epics are defined in a follow-up\n  decomposition once the target tools are ratified; the prioritized list also\n  grounds the whitepaper's enterprise-tooling guidance.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48418,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c6f096221755416","agent_id":"a146aba0fdbcda8ca","session_id":"fedb8ce9-e0a4-4a22-8d10-7c9db2355a36","uuid":"0df9c6dd-cea2-469c-8805-39a61acc33b1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:58:48.697Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9008"}
