{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-863df135ef093d30","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9008\n3\tscore: 12\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: Type Correctness\n9\t  description: E004 lists Investigations E002 and E003 in dependencies but gated_by\n10\t    (single-valued) records only E001, and gate_failure_impact covers only the administration-direction\n11\t    failure; extend the fallback_approach to state the handling when the E002 onboarding-scope\n12\t    or E003 target-tool-list gates fail or stall (rewrite/hold the corresponding whitepaper\n13\t    sections).\n14\t- severity: minor\n15\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n16\t  description: 'E002 human_judgment_required=-1 is arguable: the onboarding-scope\n17\t    ratification is the strategy open question gating both phase-2 scoping and the\n18\t    whitepaper onboarding sections, so the rubric condition for -2 (gating question\n19\t    is itself a human/product decision) applies at least as strongly as the recorded\n20\t    peripheral-decision reading.'\n21\terror: null\n22\t---\n23\t## Review Summary\n24\t\n25\tScore: 12/14 — pass\n26\tRecommendation: accept\n27\t\n28\tDecomposition of RHAISTRAT-9008 (4 epics: 3 Investigations + 1 docs-authoring\n29\tImplementation). The unbounded-outcome phased path is the correct treatment for\n30\ta strategy whose HLR-1..HLR-3 are contradictory or undefined. Two minor\n31\tgating/scoring nits; no critical or major issues. Contract validator: OK.\n32\t\n33\t## Criterion Details\n34\t\n35\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n36\t\n37\tAll four HLRs map to at least one epic, and the traceability matrix in the\n38\tdecomposition summary is present and complete: HLR-1 → E001, HLR-2 → E002,\n39\tHLR-3 → E003 (each covered by the investigation that resolves the unknown\n40\tblocking its implementation), HLR-4 → E004 (direct coverage). Every epic's\n