7\tE002's ratified scope definition, journey map, per-stage breakdown, and\n138\tfriction split; E003's consolidated feedback, candidate tool list, integration\n139\tinventory, and ratified prioritized list; E004's approved outline, consistency\n140\twith ratified outcomes, technical review sign-off, and publication reference.\n141\tThe docs-authoring rule-mandated AC (technical review with recorded sign-off)\n142\tis present in E004. No replacement or konflux-chain epics exist, so no other\n143\trule-mandated ACs apply. No AC states an external schedule constraint (the\n144\tstrategy's turnaround/timing concerns are correctly held in Health Warnings).\n145\tNo epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — only HLR numbers and\n146\tfrontmatter fields.\n147\t\n148\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n149\t\n150\tCombined epic set accounts for all strategy scope: the three contradictory or\n151\tundefined HLRs each get the investigation that unblocks them, and the one\n152\tfully specified deliverable (HLR-4 whitepaper) is implemented directly. All\n153\tthree strategy open questions are carried forward as the gating questions of\n154\tE001-E003 rather than silently dropped. Strategy-level context is preserved:\n155\tunconsolidated/contradictory feedback (consolidation is in each\n156\tinvestigation's scope), the empty out-of-scope statement (scope-trap warning\n157\t#4), the leadership-visibility pressure (warning #5), and missing strategy\n158\tsections (warning #1). The affected components Dashboard and Notebooks both\n159\tappear in the epic set (E002's journey mapping covers the Notebooks/workbench\n160\tsurface). The strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates section, so no\n161\tDocumentation Support obligation beyond HLR-4 itself — which E004 fulfills.\n162\tNo conditional branches are used; the unbounded-outcome phased path is the\n163\trule-sanctioned alternative and the phase-2 obligation is recorded.\n164\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bac7a76bcf9