{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aacb531eff53d0a2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E002\n3\ttitle: Define data-scientist onboarding scope and baseline where onboarding time is\n4\t  spent today\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n6\tcomponent: Dashboard\n7\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 0\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Define data-scientist onboarding scope and baseline where onboarding time is spent today\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThe strategy sets a target — onboarding a new data scientist should take \"less\n31\tthan a day\" — without defining what onboarding includes or measuring where the\n32\tday is currently spent. Until the scope is defined and the current state is\n33\tbaselined, no implementation epic can be responsibly scoped: the fix differs\n34\tcompletely depending on whether the time goes to cluster access, project\n35\tsetup, first workbench, or first deployed model. This investigation defines\n36\tthe onboarding boundary, maps the current journey, and produces a per-stage\n37\ttime breakdown with ranked bottlenecks. Its findings scope the phase-2\n38\timplementation epics and ground the onboarding best practices in the\n39\tenterprise usability whitepaper.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Obtain a ratified definition of what \"onboarding a new data scientist\"\n44\t  covers for the less-than-a-day target: which of cluster access, project\n45\t  setup, first workbench, and first deployed model count as onboarding (a\n46\t  product decision, recorded with rationale).\n47\t- Map the current end-to-end onboarding journey as a new data scientist\n48\t  experiences it — from account/project request through project creation in\n49\t  the Dashboard console, workbench spawn, and first productive notebook\n50\t  session — identifying the responsible platform surface for each stage\n51\t  (Dashboard console, Notebooks/workbench tooling, customer-side or\n52\t  platform-side administration).\n53\t- Measure or estimate the current time spent per stage, based on the\n54\t  documented flow, walkthroughs of a representative environment, and field\n55\t  feedback, and rank the bottlenecks (wait time vs. manual steps vs.\n56\t  comprehension/learning time).\n57\t- Distinguish friction that is within platform control from friction that is\n58\t  external (customer-side approvals, cluster capacity, procurement).\n59\t- Produce a findings report: the ratified onboarding scope, the per-stage time\n60\t  breakdown, the ranked bottlenecks, and candidate improvement areas with the\n61\t  affected platform surface for each — suitable for scoping implementation\n62\t  epics.\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- A ratified definition of the onboarding scope exists, stating which stages\n67\t  (cluster access, project setup, first workbench, first deployed model) count\n68\t  toward the less-than-a-day target.\n69\t- The current onboarding journey is documented stage by stage, with the\n70\t  responsible platform surface or external party identified for each stage.\n71\t- A per-stage time breakdown exists for the current state, with the dominant\n72\t  bottleneck(s) identified and the evidence for each figure recorded.\n73\t- The findings explicitly separate platform-controllable friction from\n74\t  external/customer-side friction.\n75\t- Candidate improvement areas are enumerated, each tagged with the platform\n76\t  surface it would touch, in enough detail to scope implementation epics.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- HLR-2 (onboarding a new data scientist should take less than a day — scope\n81\t  undefined): this investigation defines the scope and baselines the current\n82\t  state that HLR-2's target is measured against. Implementation epics are\n83\t  defined in a follow-up decomposition against the ranked bottlenecks; the\n84\t  findings also ground the whitepaper's onboarding guidance.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bac7a76bcf97691f","agent_id":"a19dea9a3635e0858","session_id":"fedb8ce9-e0a4-4a22-8d10-7c9db2355a36","uuid":"b14142bc-75b8-42c0-a573-d1818c72ed8e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:05:32.962Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aacb531eff53d0a2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
