{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd0390cc4ce77162","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\n3\ttitle: Resolve conflicting administration-experience requirements and set the configuration\n4\t  direction\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n6\tcomponent: Dashboard\n7\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Resolve conflicting administration-experience requirements and set the configuration direction\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThe strategy's administration requirement is self-contradictory: one strategic\n31\taccount wants fewer configuration options exposed (\"too many knobs\") while\n32\tanother explicitly wants more fine-grained controls per project. The feedback\n33\tarrived through different channels, was never consolidated, and no precedence\n34\trule exists. This investigation consolidates the account feedback, inventories\n35\tthe administration configuration surface RHOAI exposes today, and obtains a\n36\tstakeholder-ratified decision on which direction the platform will pursue\n37\t(curated simplicity, per-project granularity, or a layered combination). Its\n38\toutcome determines which administration implementation epics exist and what\n39\tthey do, and grounds the administration guidance in the enterprise usability\n40\twhitepaper.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Consolidate all administration-related feedback from strategic accounts and\n45\t  field channels into a single record with per-account attribution, surfacing\n46\t  every concrete statement about configuration complexity and control\n47\t  granularity.\n48\t- Inventory the administration configuration surface RHOAI exposes today:\n49\t  Dashboard-administered feature flags, platform defaults, and per-component\n50\t  settings (for example the OdhDashboardConfig-managed options, including\n51\t  workbench culling administration) — which knobs exist, where they are\n52\t  administered, and which are commonly used vs. rarely touched.\n53\t- Identify which accounts provided which requirement and the business weight\n54\t  behind each (account tier, renewal exposure, number of affected users).\n55\t- Draft a decision record presenting the bounded option set: (a) simplify by\n56\t  curating defaults and reducing exposed options, (b) add per-project\n57\t  fine-grained controls, (c) a layered approach that curates defaults while\n58\t  offering opt-in per-project granularity — with the trade-offs, migration\n59\t  impact on existing deployments, and effort profile of each.\n60\t- Obtain a stakeholder/product ruling on precedence and direction; record the\n61\t  decision, its rationale, and which requirement (if either) is declined or\n62\t  deferred.\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- All administration-related feedback from strategic accounts is consolidated\n67\t  into a single document with per-account attribution and source channel.\n68\t- A complete inventory of currently exposed administration configuration\n69\t  options exists, grouped by administering surface, with usage notes where\n70\t  available.\n71\t- A decision record is ratified by the product/stakeholder owners naming the\n72\t  chosen direction (simplify / per-project granularity / layered), with\n73\t  rationale and explicitly declined or deferred alternatives.\n74\t- The ratified decision identifies which downstream usability work is enabled,\n75\t  changed, or dropped as a result, in enough detail to scope implementation\n76\t  epics.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- HLR-1 (administration should be simpler — conflicting account requirements):\n81\t  this investigation resolves the conflict that currently makes HLR-1\n82\t  unimplementable. Implementation epics are defined in a follow-up\n83\t  decomposition once the direction is ratified; the ratified direction and the\n84\t  consolidated feedback record also ground the whitepaper's administration\n85\t  guidance.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-911da1c170635ad9","agent_id":"a72c63146fcb16e0c","session_id":"fedb8ce9-e0a4-4a22-8d10-7c9db2355a36","uuid":"b746862d-0dc3-45cd-83a6-1d46639fadb2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:06:45.840Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd0390cc4ce77162","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9008"}
